#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# im_part

#% text
# `im_part(z)` gives the imaginary part of the complex number `z`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Every real number has the exact imaginary part 0, also machine reals. Symbols stay unevaluated unless the assumptions make them real.

#% item
# `im_part` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
im_part(3 + 4*im)
#% output
#= 4

#% cell
im_part(2.5)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
im_part(exp(im*pi/3))
#% output
#= (1/2)*3^(1/2)

#% cell
im_part([1 + im, 2 - 3*im])
#% output
#= [1, -3]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# A real symbol:

#% cell
assuming(element(x, reals), refine(im_part(x + 2*im)))
#% output
#= 2

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `z == re(z) + im*im_part(z)`:

#% cell
z = 2.5 - 1.5*im; re(z) + im*im_part(z)
#% output
#= 2.5 - 1.5im

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `re`, `abs`, `arg`, `conjugate`
